INT. PICKLE BRINING CELLAR - DAY

Oak barrels stacked to the rafters. A single bare bulb swings on a cord. The smell is dill, vinegar and old secrets.

FELIX BRANDT, fifties, a deli owner in a stained apron and a bow tie he refuses to remove, stands guard over a barrel with both arms spread wide.

MABEL TOOMEY, thirties, a health inspector with a clipboard and a face like a closed door, taps her pen against the barrel lid.

SOL KAPLAN, sixties, Felix's brother-in-law, sits on an upturned crate eating a pickle with great concentration.

MABEL
Open the barrel, Mr. Brandt.

FELIX
It's a pickle barrel. You've seen one. They're all the same.

MABEL
Open it.

FELIX
(to the room)
Folks, nobody panic, the lady wants to see a pickle.

Sol chews. Nobody moves. The bulb sways.

SOL
(to himself)
Forty years. Forty years and she wants to see a pickle.

MABEL
I heard a noise from this barrel when I came in.

FELIX
That's fermentation. It's alive. Like all of us.

MABEL
It said "Felix."

FELIX
Then it's a very friendly pickle.

Mabel reaches for the lid. Felix steps in front of it. Sol quietly slides his crate three feet to the left, to block the door.

FELIX (CONT'D)
Mabel, may I call you Mabel, the cellar is cold, your hands are cold, come upstairs, have a bagel.

MABEL
Mr. Brandt, one thing at a time.

FELIX
I'll give you two bagels.

SOL
(to nobody)
Three. She looks like a three.

MABEL
I do not take bribes.

FELIX
Nobody said bribe. We said bagels.

FELIX
It's a family recipe, you understand!

MABEL ^
I understand a violation when I smell one!

The lid thumps from inside. All three stare at it. Sol takes another bite.

SOL
(to the group)
Nice acoustics down here.

Felix puts a hand on the lid and presses down, smiling so hard his bow tie quivers.

FELIX
Sol. The jar of the good relish. Upstairs. Now.

SOL
(rising, not hurrying)
She'll want it with mustard.

MABEL
I want the barrel open.

FELIX
And I want a bigger deli. We don't always get.

The lid thumps again. Mabel, without taking her eyes off Felix, writes one word on her clipboard and underlines it twice.
